    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Aside from unreasonably increasing the value of trunc_width , is there a way to get the short output for sections in the status line? \nFor instance, fileinfo returns filetype, encoding, format and file size. however what I'm only interested in seeing are just filetype and encoding. Same goes for location — line number & column ",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Aside from unreasonably increasing the value of trunc_width , is there a way to get the short output for sections in the status line?<br>\nFor instance, fileinfo returns filetype, encoding, format and file size. however what I'm only interested in seeing are just filetype and encoding. Same goes for location — line number &amp; column</p>",
    "bodyText": "Aside from unreasonably increasing the value of trunc_width , is there a way to get the short output for sections in the status line?\nFor instance, fileinfo returns filetype, encoding, format and file size. however what I'm only interested in seeing are just filetype and encoding. Same goes for location — line number & column",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-01-18T09:52:31Z",
    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Aside from unreasonably increasing the value of trunc_width , is there a way to get the short output for sections in the status line?\r\n\r\nAn answer to the exact question is a \"No\". However, most of the sections are more or less thin wrappers around built-in 'statuslin' syntax. So...\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> For instance, fileinfo returns filetype, encoding, format and file size. however what I'm only interested in seeing are just filetype and encoding.\r\n\r\nInstead of `section_fileinfo()`, use something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal fileinfo = vim.bo.filetype\r\n\r\nif fileinfo ~= '' then\r\n  fileinfo = string.format('%s %s[%s]', fileinfo, vim.bo.fileencoding or vim.bo.encoding, vim.bo.fileformat)\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nSee [`section_fileinfo()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/44a3ab2bc6b40edeb7a76359826c9779d5c70cb5/lua/mini/statusline.lua#L400-L419) code for more details.\r\n> Same goes for location — line number & column\r\n\r\nInstead of using `section_location`, use [`'%l│%2v'`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/44a3ab2bc6b40edeb7a76359826c9779d5c70cb5/lua/mini/statusline.lua#L434) string directly.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Aside from unreasonably increasing the value of trunc_width , is there a way to get the short output for sections in the status line?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">An answer to the exact question is a \"No\". However, most of the sections are more or less thin wrappers around built-in 'statuslin' syntax. So...</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For instance, fileinfo returns filetype, encoding, format and file size. however what I'm only interested in seeing are just filetype and encoding.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">section_fileinfo()</code>, use something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local fileinfo = vim.bo.filetype\n\nif fileinfo ~= '' then\n  fileinfo = string.format('%s %s[%s]', fileinfo, vim.bo.fileencoding or vim.bo.encoding, vim.bo.fileformat)\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">fileinfo</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bo</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">filetype</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">fileinfo</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">~=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">fileinfo</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">string.format</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%s %s[%s]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">fileinfo</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bo</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fileencoding</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bo</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">encoding</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bo</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fileformat</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/44a3ab2bc6b40edeb7a76359826c9779d5c70cb5/lua/mini/statusline.lua#L400-L419\"><code class=\"notranslate\">section_fileinfo()</code></a> code for more details.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Same goes for location — line number &amp; column</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Instead of using <code class=\"notranslate\">section_location</code>, use <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/44a3ab2bc6b40edeb7a76359826c9779d5c70cb5/lua/mini/statusline.lua#L434\"><code class=\"notranslate\">'%l│%2v'</code></a> string directly.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Aside from unreasonably increasing the value of trunc_width , is there a way to get the short output for sections in the status line?\n\nAn answer to the exact question is a \"No\". However, most of the sections are more or less thin wrappers around built-in 'statuslin' syntax. So...\n\nFor instance, fileinfo returns filetype, encoding, format and file size. however what I'm only interested in seeing are just filetype and encoding.\n\nInstead of section_fileinfo(), use something like this:\nlocal fileinfo = vim.bo.filetype\n\nif fileinfo ~= '' then\n  fileinfo = string.format('%s %s[%s]', fileinfo, vim.bo.fileencoding or vim.bo.encoding, vim.bo.fileformat)\nend\nSee section_fileinfo() code for more details.\n\nSame goes for location — line number & column\n\nInstead of using section_location, use '%l│%2v' string directly.",
