            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "Sorry to revive an old question, but when you say \"Instead of ..., use something like: ...\", how does one put that in say a mini.statusline.lua or lazy.lua or init.lua? From `:set statusline` I get:\r\n```\r\nstatusline=%{%(nvim_get_current_win()==#g:actual_curwin || &laststatus==3) ? v:lua.MiniStatusline.active() : v:lua.MiniStatusline.inactive()%}\r\n```\r\nwould it be best to change what `active()` function does? Redefine it after loading mini.statusline?",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry to revive an old question, but when you say \"Instead of ..., use something like: ...\", how does one put that in say a mini.statusline.lua or lazy.lua or init.lua? From <code class=\"notranslate\">:set statusline</code> I get:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"statusline=%{%(nvim_get_current_win()==#g:actual_curwin || &amp;laststatus==3) ? v:lua.MiniStatusline.active() : v:lua.MiniStatusline.inactive()%}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">statusline=%{%(nvim_get_current_win()==#g:actual_curwin || &amp;laststatus==3) ? v:lua.MiniStatusline.active() : v:lua.MiniStatusline.inactive()%}\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">would it be best to change what <code class=\"notranslate\">active()</code> function does? Redefine it after loading mini.statusline?</p>",
            "bodyText": "Sorry to revive an old question, but when you say \"Instead of ..., use something like: ...\", how does one put that in say a mini.statusline.lua or lazy.lua or init.lua? From :set statusline I get:\nstatusline=%{%(nvim_get_current_win()==#g:actual_curwin || &laststatus==3) ? v:lua.MiniStatusline.active() : v:lua.MiniStatusline.inactive()%}\n\nwould it be best to change what active() function does? Redefine it after loading mini.statusline?",
